The week ahead

We kick off the live sport next week with Premier League action, as Nuno Es=
p=C3=ADrito Santo steps into the West Ham hotseat with a trip to Everton at=
 8pm (all times BST) on Monday.


Into Tuesday and we have more football for you as Liverpool head to Istanbu=
l to take on Galatasaray, where they will be afforded a customary warm welc=
ome by the Turkish champions' fanatical supporters for the
Champions League
tie. Kick-off for that one is 8pm. At the same time, we'll have a live cloc=
kwatch covering all the goals in the night's other European matches.


The
Women's Cricket World Cup
in India will already be under way by Wednesday =E2=80=93 and we'll bring y=
ou over-by-over updates on the keenly anticipated match between reigning ch=
ampions Australia and New Zealand at the Holkar Stadium from 10.30am.


There is more
Champions League
football later on Wednesday as Union-Saint Gilloise host Newcastle at 5.45p=
m, before Arsenal v Olympiakos at 8pm as our clockwatch takes in Barcelona =
v PSG. There is a stacked list of
Europa League
fixtures on Thursday and we'll provide goal updates from across the night, =
with an intriguing tussle as Nottingham Forest host Porto.


On Friday, England get their
Women's Cricket World Cup
campaign under way against South Africa. The team have struggled for form s=
ince the 2022 tournament and will be looking to turn around their flagging =
fortunes. On the football side of things, we'll provide news updates with o=
ur live blog through the day and bring you minute-by-minute updates on Manc=
hester United v Chelsea in the
WSL
at 7.30pm.


To the weekend, and on Saturday we have our
matchday live
football blog live from 8am, with discussion and buildup to the day's big g=
ames. These include Manchester City v Arsenal (midday) in the
WSL
and Leeds v Tottenham (12.30pm) and Chelsea v Liverpool (5.30pm) in the
Premier League
. We will have minute-by-minute coverage of all three games and a clockwatc=
h covering the 3pm kick-offs in the UK and beyond. There will also be lap-b=
y-lap updates on Singapore GP qualifying (1pm) as the
F1
season gets closer to the business end.


On Sunday our
matchday live
football blog will crank into action at 8am and run through till 2.30pm, ta=
king in the lunchtime kick-offs in the
WSL
. There are four
Premier League
games at 2pm, and we'll have goal updates in our clockwatch through the aft=
ernoon before our focus switches to a bespoke minute-by-minute report on Br=
entford v Manchester City (4.30pm). We'll also be covering the
Prix l'Arc de Triomphe
, with the race meeting starting at midday, and the Singapore GP race prope=
r in
F1
at 2pm.


